# These files are deployed as they are onto Linux, and claw/ onto a busybox
# board that refuses CRLF outright. core.autocrlf=true is set on kil's PC, so
# without these rules a fresh clone converts them and the deployment fails in a
# way that says nothing useful (/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter).
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.conf     text eol=lf
*.service  text eol=lf
vodloopctl text eol=lf
# By name is not enough here: everything the board runs is extensionless, and
# S98vodloopwatch had already slipped through these rules. The directory is the
# rule, so nothing added to it later has to remember to ask.
claw/*     text eol=lf
# v2: the board runs these through busybox sh, which refuses CRLF outright.
v2/claw/*  text eol=lf

# Ce depot se deploie par scp depuis Windows: un fichier livre doit partir
# comme il est commite, sinon la copie de travail expedie des CRLF a Linux.
*.py       text eol=lf
